1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,622
Three charts. Three new skills to test.

2
00:00:02,991 --> 00:00:05,001
Trends, candles and trade plans.

3
00:00:05,501 --> 00:00:08,605
Question one. It's choppy, with some deep pullbacks.

4
00:00:08,953 --> 00:00:11,625
Is this an uptrend, a downtrend, or a range?

5
00:00:15,475 --> 00:00:16,303
An uptrend.

6
00:00:16,711 --> 00:00:21,743
Follow the swings, not the noise. Each high is higher than the last, and so is each low.

7
00:00:22,475 --> 00:00:26,099
Question two. After a long run up, three candles are marked.

8
00:00:26,437 --> 00:00:29,091
Which one was the warning sign? A, B, or C?

9
00:00:32,941 --> 00:00:33,438
B.

10
00:00:33,832 --> 00:00:43,640
A big red candle swallowed the one before it, at the top of a long run, on heavy volume. One candle is never a guarantee, but it's a clue worth respecting.

11
00:00:44,140 --> 00:00:49,200
Question three. Same entry, two plans. Green is the target, red is the stop.

12
00:00:49,573 --> 00:00:51,220
Is plan A better, or plan B?

13
00:00:55,070 --> 00:00:55,777
Plan B.

14
00:00:56,114 --> 00:01:03,981
Plan A risks as much as it can make. Plan B risks a little to make several times more. You can be wrong more often, and still come out ahead.

15
00:01:04,481 --> 00:01:07,225
How many did you get? Tell me your score in the comments.

16
00:01:07,615 --> 00:01:11,247
Practise on real charts from the game, at memestreet.net.

